From a2eb40f6d7e205a96bd6100b76204f53209a5166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:03:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Re-apply the five S08/S17 audit fixes lost in the
 upstream merge; fix a sixth defect the merge introduced
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PRs #113-#116 merged the S08/S17 content from their pre-audit form.
The five reviewer fixes from the audited branch were dropped; all five
defects reproduced on main and are re-applied here, plus one NEW
miscompile introduced by #116's own regparm capture:

1. Backend scalar FMA fusion (x86 vfmadd231s{s,d}, AArch64 fmadd) now
   respects -ffp-contract: CodegenOptions.fp_contract_fast gates
   supports_fused_float_mul_add on both backends. Before: contract=off
   still fused (single-rounding contract silently broken).

2. Contraction default = fast (GCC gnu-C parity, verified vs gcc 14.2),
   explicit -ffp-contract sticky against -ffast-math in both orders
   (GCC opts_set semantics), -fno-fast-math restores the default
   rather than forcing off. CLI tests extended to pin all four
   configurations.

3. detect_mul_add_fusions soundness: the fused sequence is emitted at
   the Mul's program point, so Copy/Cast instructions skipped between
   Mul and Add must not define an Add operand (post-phi
   `Copy acc_read <- acc_phi` shape read the accumulator one iteration
   stale). nbody -O0 printed -0.3248 on main; now -0.169075164 at all
   opt levels.

4. i686 compare immediates normalized to operand width+signedness:
   (unsigned char)255 == (char)-1 emitted `cmpl $-1,%eax` against a
   movzbl-extended 255 — always false. Both emit_int_cmp and the fused
   compare-branch normalize now (mirrors operand_to_eax's extension).

5. emit_avx_reduction_fma fallback staged the accumulator in ymm2 =
   PhysReg(20), the first ALLOCATABLE SIMD register (clobber hazard
   when the dest itself missed allocation); now reserved ymm1.

6. NEW (#116): the merged "capture regparm incoming EAX/EDX/ECX" loop
   re-captured params already saved by the phase-1/2 capture pass.
   The second capture runs interleaved with stack-param copies that
   stage through %eax, so it stored the STACK param's copied value
   over the register argument: d_i(double a, int b) read b as garbage
   at -O1+ (regparm conformance bit 5). The loop now skips
   param_pre_stored entries.

Validation: 831/831 unit, 50/50 correctness, 9/9 codegen scripts,
regparm+cdecl ABI matrix green at -O0..-Os, nbody correct at all
levels, contract matrix identical to gcc 14.2.
